course: dictionary
lesson: 4848
title: A word with a song inside
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A hymn is a song of praise. Praise means saying how good or wonderful something is. Most hymns are sung to God in church, but children can also sing them in assembly and people sing them at other religious events.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Charles wrote thousands of hymns» tells you a hymn is something a person can write, like a poem with a tune. «Hymns are songs to God; at funerals they give comfort and hope» tells you what hymns are for.
explain: The word can also be used in a wider way, as in «a hymn to freedom». Here a hymn is a song or piece that praises freedom. The clue is the words after "to". Try the swap check: "a song of praise to freedom" still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
fact: A hymn is a song of praise, often sung in church.
fact: A hymn book is a book that holds hymns, and a hymn sheet is a page with hymns printed on it.
fact: «Sing from the same hymn sheet» means that people agree with each other.
fact: Charles Wesley wrote thousands of hymns, and he helped start the Methodist Church in the 1700s.
fact: «The Lord's my shepherd», based on Psalm 23, is a hymn that is often sung.
exercise: «The Methodist Church was started by John and Charles Wesley in the 1700s; Charles wrote thousands of hymns.» What is a hymn in this sentence? | *A song of praise, sung to God | A prayer said quietly at school | A kind of church building | A helper who looks after a church
exercise: «Hymns are songs to God; at funerals they give comfort and hope.» What do hymns give at funerals? | A long, boring talk | *Comfort and hope | Loud bells and fireworks | Money and new shoes
exercise: The poet wrote «a hymn to freedom». What does hymn mean here? | A quiet walk in the park | A book about the weather | A list of rules about freedom | *A song or piece praising freedom
test: «In the end he owned up to all of it, went to confession, said sorry to the churchwarden and paid for a new hymn book from his pocket money.» What is a hymn book? | A cookbook with recipes | A book about pets | A notebook for maths | *A book that holds hymns
test: «Sing from the same hymn sheet» means what? | Sit in neat rows | *Agree with each other | Sing very loudly | Forget all the words
exam: Which one is a song sung to God? | *A hymn | A confession | A churchwarden | Pocket money
